    "answer": {
      "short": "$P(t)=\\dfrac{900}{1+8e^{-t/3}}$. After 6 years, approximately $432$ fish.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{dt}{dP}&=\\frac{2700}{P(900-P)}\\\\\\frac{dt}{dP}&=3\\left(\\frac1P+\\frac1{900-P}\\right)\\\\t&=3\\bigl(\\ln|P|-\\ln|900-P|\\bigr)+D\\\\\\ln\\left|\\frac{P}{900-P}\\right|&=\\frac{t-D}{3}\\\\\\frac{P}{900-P}&=Ae^{t/3}\\end{align*}$$\nUsing $P(0)=100$,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{100}{900-100}&=Ae^0\\\\A&=\\frac18.\\end{align*}$$\nHence\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{P}{900-P}&=\\frac18e^{t/3}\\\\8P&=(900-P)e^{t/3}\\\\P(8+e^{t/3})&=900e^{t/3}\\\\P(t)&=\\frac{900e^{t/3}}{8+e^{t/3}}\\\\P(t)&=\\frac{900}{1+8e^{-t/3}}.\\end{align*}$$\nAfter 6 years,\n$$\\begin{align*}P(6)&=\\frac{900}{1+8e^{-2}}\\\\P(6)&\\approx432\\text{ fish}.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
